.TH ECL-POST 1 "2026-09-23" "ecl-client 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ecl-post \- post an entry to a Fermilab Electronic Logbook (ECL)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ecl-post
.RB [ \-i
.IR NAME " | " \-U " " URL ]
.RB [ \-u
.IR USER ]
.B \-c
.I CATEGORY
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B ecl-post \-\-dry-run \-c
.I CATEGORY
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ecl-post
builds an ECL 8.x XML entry and submits it with
.PP
.RS
.B POST
.IB instance /E/xml_post?salt= random
.RE
.PP
Entries may carry a subject, body text, category path, tags, form fields,
file attachments, image attachments, a related entry and a private flag.
On success the new entry ID and the final endpoint URL are printed on
standard output.
.PP
Fermilab instance URLs answer with a 303 redirect to an active backend.
.B ecl-post
keeps the POST method and the exact signed body across up to five
redirects, recomputing the signature when the query string changes.
Cross-host redirects are accepted only between hosts under
.IR fnal.gov .
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Connection and authentication
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-instance " " \fINAME\fR
ECL instance alias. Expands to
.BI https://dbweb0.fnal.gov/ECL/ NAME\fR.
Aliases are lower case, for example
.BR mu2e ,
.BR nova ,
.BR demo .
A value containing
.B ://
is used verbatim.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-url " " \fIURL\fR
Full instance URL. Takes precedence over
.BR \-\-instance .
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-username " " \fIUSER\fR
ECL account name.
.TP
.BR \-\-auth " " xml | password
.B xml
(default) sends the username and an MD5 digest of the query string, raw API
password and XML body in ECL headers; the password is never transmitted.
Requires an ECL XML/API account.
.B password
sends username and password in ECL headers and is permitted only over HTTPS.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " PATH"
Read configuration from
.I PATH
instead of the default. An explicitly named file must exist.
.TP
.BI \-\-timeout " SECONDS"
Overall request timeout (default 30).
.TP
.BI \-\-connect\-timeout " SECONDS"
Connection timeout (default 10).
.TP
.B \-\-insecure
Disable TLS certificate and hostname verification. Diagnostics only.
.SS Entry content
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-category " " \fIPATH\fR
Category path, for example
.BR Operations/DAQ .
Required. Paths are case sensitive and specific to each instance.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-subject " " \fITEXT\fR
Entry subject.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-text " " \fITEXT\fR
Entry body.
.TP
.BR \-T ", " \-\-text\-file " " \fIPATH\fR
Read the body from
.IR PATH ;
.B \-
reads standard input. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-text .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-form " " \fINAME\fR
Form name (default
.BR default ).
.TP
.BR \-\-format " " plain | textile | preformatted
Body markup (default
.BR plain ).
.TP
.BI \-\-tag " TAG"
Add a tag. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-field " NAME" = VALUE
Set a form field. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-\-attachment " [" \fINAME\fR = "]" \fIPATH\fR
Attach a file. Without
.IR NAME ,
the file's basename is used. Repeatable.
.TP
.BR \-\-image " [" \fINAME\fR = "]" \fIPATH\fR
Attach an image. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-\-related " ID"
Link the entry to existing entry
.IR ID .
.TP
.B \-\-private
Mark the entry private.
.SS Miscellaneous
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print the generated XML and exit. No credentials, URL or network access are
needed.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the library version and exit.
.PP
There is intentionally no password option; command-line arguments are visible
in process listings and shell history.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Precedence, highest first: command-line options, environment variables,
configuration file, built-in defaults.
.PP
The default file is
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ecl-client/config ,
or
.I ~/.config/ecl-client/config
when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset. It contains
.IB key = value
lines; blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored. Recognised keys:
.BR url ", " instance ", " username ", " password ", " auth ", "
.BR category ", " form ", " format ", " timeout ", " connect_timeout .
.PP
A file containing
.B password
must not be readable or writable by group or others (mode 0600), otherwise
.B ecl-post
refuses to run.
.PP
If no password is found,
.B ecl-post
prompts on
.I /dev/tty
with echo disabled.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ECL_URL
Instance URL.
.TP
.B ECL_INSTANCE
Instance alias.
.TP
.B ECL_USERNAME
Account name.
.TP
.B ECL_PASSWORD
Account or API password.
.TP
.B ECL_AUTH
.BR xml " or " password .
.TP
.B ECL_CATEGORY
Default category path.
.TP
.B ECL_FORM
Default form name.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the default configuration file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Entry created, or dry run / help / version completed.
.TP
.B 1
Library error: HTTP failure, protocol error, I/O error while reading an
attachment, or rejected redirect.
.TP
.B 2
Usage or configuration error.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect the XML without contacting ECL:
.PP
.RS
.nf
ecl-post \-n \-c Sandbox \-s 'Test' \-t 'Hello' \-\-tag test
.fi
.RE
.PP
Post to the Mu2e logbook with an attachment:
.PP
.RS
.nf
export ECL_USERNAME=automation-account
read \-rs ECL_PASSWORD; export ECL_PASSWORD
ecl-post \-i mu2e \-c Sandbox \-s 'Automated status' \e
    \-T status.txt \-\-tag automated \-\-attachment report=report.json
.fi
.RE
.PP
Post a generated report from standard input to NOvA with password
authentication:
.PP
.RS
.nf
generate-report | ecl-post \-i nova \-\-auth password \e
    \-c Sandbox \-s 'Generated report' \-T \-
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ecl-client/config
Default configuration file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ecl (3),
.BR ecl_client (3)
.PP
Fermilab ECL instance directory:
.I https://dbweb0.fnal.gov/redirector/ecl_instances.html
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman <anorman@fnal.gov>
